      "message": "Hey, this commit actually breaks the NFC driver and causes NFC to be not recognized by the system (not appear in the system settings menu at all). Upon a deeper investigation, I found out why this issue occurred:\n\nLineageOS’s Soong config ([vendor/lineage/config/BoardConfigSoong.mk#L76](https://github.com/LineageOS/android_vendor_lineage/blob/2806ce8d99bb3136acc04c6641988128370d89b4/config/BoardConfigSoong.mk#L70)) always fallbacks to `TARGET_INIT_VENDOR_LIB` if the flag is set. Since sm8250-common still sets this variable [android_device_xiaomi_sm8250/BoardConfigCommon.mk#L81](https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_xiaomi_sm8250-common/tree/4e2eafde897f6dc07c06b1b1f3998e7055a148fc), and cmi build script no longer does after the migration (commit 820e726), BoardConfigSoong ends up re-initializing the wrong vendor init using the common device\u0027s init file at the end, overriding cmi\u0027s device vendor init via soong done in `device.mk`. This breaks NFC on the device.\n\nAs a temporary workaround, resetting the flag to empty by adding the line `TARGET_INIT_VENDOR_LIB :\u003d `(empty) in cmi’s BoardConfig.mk overrides the flag from the common device config, fixing the issue (tested and confirmed). Although ideally, this should be addressed by migrating the Makefile vendor init in sm8250-common.",
